|~ What is declared under `::proj`, the step that reads a part of a
   value: the refusals of a read that misses. ~|

:proj/construct |~~ The step of a projection from its record, `:path`, which reads back as itself. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:proj/PayloadNotSchemaError
  |~~ A `::proj` is a map of `:path`, a vector of keys and
      integers.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        ::proj{:path "items"}
        !| [type /field]
        |  eq [::proj/PayloadNotSchemaError :path]
       )
  ~~|

:proj/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::proj` prints as text that reads back as another step: a
      key that reads as an index is written as the index.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        ::proj{:path [:"0"]}
        !| [type /printed]
        |  eq [::proj/ReadBackDiffersError "/\"0\""]
       )
  ~~|

:proj/IndexOutOfBoundsError
  |~~ An index reads within a vector or a set, from `/0` to the last,
      `/-1`; `take` and `drop` answer the part there is without refusing.
      `:length` holds the length of the subject.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        [10 20 30] | /99
        !| [type /index /length]
        |  eq [::proj/IndexOutOfBoundsError 99 3]
       )
  ~~|

:proj/KeyNotInMapError
  |~~ A projection names a key the map holds, so a misspelled field is
      found where it is read; `keys` lists the keys there are, and
      `at :key` answers null for a key that may be absent.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        {:a 1} | /b
        !| [type /key]
        |  eq [::proj/KeyNotInMapError "b"]
       )
  ~~|

:proj/SubjectNotProjectableError
  |~~ A projection reads a part of a map, a vector or a set, one under a
      tag among them; a number, a string or null has no parts, and a map
      that may lack a key is read by `at`, which answers null for it.
      A modifier reads the subject of its own step: after `/qty |` the
      subject is the number, so two parts of one record are read in one
      step by a form whose objects they are, `mulOf /qty /price`.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~({:qty 2 :price 3} | /qty | mul /price !| type | eq ::proj/SubjectNotProjectableError)
      ~({:qty 2 :price 3} | mulOf /qty /price | eq 6)

      ~(
        42 | /foo
        !| [type /key /actualType]
        |  eq [::proj/SubjectNotProjectableError "foo" ::number]
       )
  ~~|

:proj/IndexNotIntegerError
  |~~ A vector is read by an index, `/0`, a set's in its one order; a
      field of each element is read under `*`, `* /name`, and the
      elements a field picks are found by `filter`.
      ::link~(::proj | doc)

      ~(
        [10 20 30] | /name
        !| [type /key]
        |  eq [::proj/IndexNotIntegerError "name"]
       )
       ~(
        #[:a :b :c] | /name
        !| [type /key]
        |  eq [::proj/IndexNotIntegerError "name"]
       )
  ~~|
